   "evidence": "Kinematics/Basic.lean:35-36 `/-- Outgoing hadron momentum in exclusive/semi-inclusive projections. For inclusive DIS this field can be carried as background data. -/ pPrime : V`; the structure's only hypothesis field is `hq : q = k - kPrime` (line 45). By contrast `ExclKinematics` does carry `hMomentum : p + q = pPrime + qPrime` (Exclusive/Kinematics/Basic.lean:52), so the repo tracks this constraint where it is meant.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Corrections/Eikonal.lean",
   "fix": "Either build the constraint in \u2014 `chargedLine K.p (K.p + K.q) eHadron`, which imposes hadronic momentum conservation `p + q = p'` by construction \u2014 and state the remaining on-shell condition `g K.pPrime K.pPrime = g K.p K.p` as an explicit hypothesis where elasticity is claimed, or drop \"elastic\" from the name and docstrings and describe them as the lepton line and hadron line of `K`.",
   "issue": "`elasticLegs` is documented as \"the charged legs of elastic lepton\u2013hadron scattering\", but `DisKinematics` (Kinematics/Basic.lean:32-45) has only `hq : q = k - kPrime`; `pPrime` is explicitly \"carried as background data\" with no relation to `p` and `q`. So `K.elasticLegs` labels four arbitrary momenta as elastic, and `netCharge_elasticLegs` (line 244, \"Elastic lepton\u2013hadron scattering conserves charge\") and `eikonalCurrent_elasticLegs_conserved` (line 259) inherit that overclaim \u2014 they hold for any data whatsoever. The roadmap acceptance item is about elastic lepton\u2013proton scattering, so the label is load-bearing for a future elastic-tail development.",
   "line": 233
  }
